## Implementations

In `MyFirstActor.cpp`:

```cpp
#include "MyFirstActor.h"

AMyFirstActor::AMyFirstActor()
{
    PrimaryActorTick.bCanEverTick = true;
}

void AMyFirstActor::BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();
    // Your code here
}

void AMyFirstActor::Tick(float DeltaTime)
{
    Super::Tick(DeltaTime);
    // Your code here
}
```
* Always call `Super::BeginPlay()` to run parent logic.
* Set `bCanEverTick = true` in the constructor if you need Tick.

## Attach Sub‑Objects

You can add components like Static Mesh, Sphere Collision, etc., in the constructor:

```cpp
AMyActor::AMyActor()
{
    PrimaryActorTick.bCanEverTick = true;

    MeshComp = CreateDefaultSubobject<UStaticMeshComponent>(TEXT("Mesh"));
    RootComponent = MeshComp;
}
```
You need to declare the component in the header:

```cpp
UPROPERTY(VisibleAnywhere)
UStaticMeshComponent* MeshComp;
```
* `CreateDefaultSubobject` creates the component.
* `RootComponent` assigns it as the root. Without this, the Actor has no transform origin.
